 <LayoutItem background="false" blendMode="0" excludeFromExports="0" frame="false" frameJoinStyle="miter" groupUuid="" halign="1" htmlState="1" id="" itemRotation="0" labelText="&lt;div style=&quot;font-family:Arial; font-size:7.5pt; line-height:1.35;&quot;>&#xa;&lt;b style=&quot;font-size:11pt;&quot;>Assessment&lt;/b>&#xa;&lt;table cellspacing=&quot;0&quot; cellpadding=&quot;3&quot; style=&quot;border-collapse:collapse; margin-top:3px;&quot;>&#xa;&lt;tr>&#xa; &lt;td width=&quot;50%&quot; bgcolor=&quot;#e5f2e5&quot; style=&quot;border:1px solid #9bbf9b;&quot;>&lt;b style=&quot;color:#1b5e20;&quot;>Strengths&lt;/b>&lt;/td>&#xa; &lt;td width=&quot;50%&quot; bgcolor=&quot;#f6e3e3&quot; style=&quot;border:1px solid #c99a9a;&quot;>&lt;b style=&quot;color:#a50f15;&quot;>Weaknesses&lt;/b>&lt;/td>&#xa;&lt;/tr>&#xa;&lt;tr>&#xa; &lt;td valign=&quot;top&quot; style=&quot;border:1px solid #9bbf9b;&quot;>&#xa; One large urban green area (58.8 ha) in the south, above the 50 ha size linked to area-sensitive species (Beninde et al., 2015)&lt;br>&lt;br>&#xa; Dense street tree network (18,536 trees) as potential corridors between parks&lt;br>&lt;br>&#xa; 1,242 species recorded, mostly in the green areas&lt;br>&lt;br>&#xa; 10 protected old trees, mostly in Westfalenpark, give shade and old-tree habitat&lt;br>&lt;br>&#xa; Green areas cool their surroundings and support species at the same time&#xa; &lt;/td>&#xa; &lt;td valign=&quot;top&quot; style=&quot;border:1px solid #c99a9a;&quot;>&#xa; 81 % of the district is sealed by built-up land and transport&lt;br>&lt;br>&#xa; Woodland only 2.6 %, in 52 small patches (largest 5.4 ha)&lt;br>&lt;br>&#xa; One connected transport network separates almost all habitat patches&lt;br>&lt;br>&#xa; No nature reserve; protection is limited to 18 ha of LSG, two protected landscape components (21.4 ha) and 10 protected old trees&lt;br>&lt;br>&#xa; Most streets are lit; dark green areas are few and isolated&#xa; &lt;/td>&#xa;&lt;/tr>&#xa;&lt;/table>&#xa;&lt;div style=&quot;margin-top:4px; color:#333333;&quot;>&lt;b>Conclusion:&lt;/b> few, small and fragmented habitats. Enlarging and connecting green areas would reduce heat and support biodiversity at the same time.&lt;/div>&#xa;&lt;/div>" marginX="0" marginY="0" opacity="1" outlineWidthM="0.3,mm" position="92.3468,140.445,mm" positionLock="false" positionOnPage="92.3468,140.445,mm" referencePoint="0" size="122.468,65.796,mm" templateUuid="{de38c482-4ea7-46a8-ac6e-172d9091a183}" type="65641" uuid="{de38c482-4ea7-46a8-ac6e-172d9091a183}" valign="32" visibility="1" zValue="8">
